---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ContentNote from '../components/content/ContentNote.astro';
import RelatedReading from '../components/content/RelatedReading.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Corrections Policy | Cooked Finance"
  description="How to report a Cooked Finance error and how we investigate, correct, annotate, and document material changes."
  path="/corrections-policy"
  eyebrow="Accountability"
  heading="Corrections should be visible, not quietly buried."
  lead="When a factual, methodological, or product error could change a reader’s understanding, we document the repair."
  updated="August 17, 2026"
>
  <h2>What to report</h2>
  <p>We welcome reports about:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>incorrect figures, definitions, formulas, units, or source descriptions;</li>
    <li>a citation that does not support the claim beside it;</li>
    <li>calculator behavior that differs from the published methodology;</li>
    <li>missing context that materially changes an interpretation;</li>
    <li>broken accessibility, privacy, or security behavior; and</li>
    <li>outdated statements presented as current.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to submit a correction</h2>
  <p>
    Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and include the page URL, the
    exact sentence or behavior, why it appears wrong, and—if available—a primary
    source or steps that reproduce the issue. Do not send account numbers,
    financial statements, passwords, or other sensitive personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>How reports are reviewed</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Reproduce the product behavior or reopen the cited source.</li>
    <li>Check the claim’s population, date, definition, units, and surrounding context.</li>
    <li>Decide whether the issue is material, minor, disputed, or unsupported.</li>
    <li>Correct the page and any affected calculator, cross-link, or explanation.</li>
    <li>Add a correction note when the original could have materially misled a reader.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Material versus minor changes</h2>
  <p>
    A <strong>material correction</strong> changes a formula, result, data value,
    source interpretation, safety implication, or central conclusion. The page
    should receive a dated note explaining what changed. A <strong>minor edit</strong>
    fixes spelling, grammar, formatting, a non-substantive broken link, or wording
    without changing meaning; it may be corrected without a formal note.
  </p>

  <ContentNote title="Updates are not corrections">
    <p>
      Replacing an older, accurately described dataset with a newly released wave
      is an update. Fixing a value that was transcribed incorrectly is a correction.
      When both happen together, the note should distinguish them.
    </p>
  </ContentNote>

  <h2>Calculator and methodology changes</h2>
  <p>
    If the model changes intentionally, the <a href="/methodology/">methodology
    version history</a> records the new version, date, and material differences.
    If code does not match the published version, that is treated as an error.
    Results from materially different model versions should not be represented as
    directly comparable.
  </p>

  <h2>Correction log</h2>
  <p>
    Material correction entries will be listed here with the date, affected page,
    original problem, and resolution. No entries are currently listed for model
    version 2.0.0.
  </p>

  <RelatedReading links={[
    { href: '/contact/', label: 'Report an issue', description: 'Send the affected URL and enough detail to verify the concern.' },
    { href: '/editorial-policy/', label: 'Editorial policy', description: 'The publication process intended to prevent avoidable errors.' },
    { href: '/source-policy/', label: 'Source policy', description: 'The checks applied to claims, tables, and external evidence.' },
  ]} />
</PageLayout>
